{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"2d6e06c31833ecf19f179a180f2e6f0be49f9c0647ad827967fe1caf5b41085c","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_84d920980877735ae09b6b4cc813b303b7672af1c4afa1434416c6468d608af2","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical contribution to machine comprehension using the SQuAD dataset. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine specific policy compliance regarding anonymity, plagiarism, or broader impact documentation, as no venue-specific policies or external overlap data are available. The paper explicitly cites the SQuAD dataset and its creators, addressing data provenance, but does not contain a dedicated ethics or broader impact statement.","paper_id":"B1-q5Pqxl","paper_identity_sha256":"f0a3523c05db60e2bbdf762391461d827fcf15b4fadeee965368011497aa49c4","prompt_identity_sha256":"9e23506805fd0a1d758223c90b45d4e42085856ad7e42760c92e87c7c19b66f4","raw_response_sha256":"2e8e71e7a25a24ac522545662d744f509c108655c9ea7ce45ffa3bfd8cdcef92","request_identity_sha256":"9f80b50ff9971c1df7e1c976a354dcb7b2bde0e17357297db5228167fe3c4e4f","reviewer_identity_sha256":"ffb7de3c92b60fd85ca4efbe762244cb204797e709b6c35d64f8aa04c356bd04","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"246e42ed15511d2829c5c387e87312a72aba34e11eccfcf439d0ef8721f75d25","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section or discussion regarding ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms associated with the proposed machine comprehension models. The focus is strictly on technical performance and model architecture. No material ethical-risk pathway is visible in the supplied text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024","SRC-032"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the Stanford Question Answering Dataset (SQuAD) v1.1, noting that passages are derived from Wikipedia articles and questions were created by humans through crowdsourcing. The authors explicitly cite the dataset creators (Rajpurkar et al., 2016) and acknowledge the source of the data. The paper does not discuss specific privacy regulations, consent mechanisms for the crowdsourced annotators, or licensing terms beyond the standard academic citation of the dataset.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper header explicitly lists the authors' names (Shuohang Wang, Jing Jiang), their institutional affiliation (Singapore Management University), and their email addresses. The acknowledgments section also names specific individuals (Pranav Rajpurkar, Percy Liang). Without a frozen venue-specific anonymity policy for the 2017 ICLR submission, it is not possible to declare a policy violation, but the presence of these identifiers is noted.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not include external plagiarism overlap data or information regarding dual submission. The paper cites prior work, including the authors' own previous work on match-LSTM (Wang & Jiang, 2016), which is standard academic practice. Absence of evidence in the corpus does not prove originality or the absence of dual submission.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. The conclusions section focuses on future technical directions rather than societal implications. Without a frozen policy obligation requiring such statements for this specific venue and year, the absence of these documents is noted as a limitation of the supplied evidence rather than a confirmed compliance failure.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"be10ec62d664479dfb6fdccf1d34271bbdac8a80fcba0edc6221f38de9c6e344","paper_id":"B1-q5Pqxl","paper_ordinal":1,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant